From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Mason <mason@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:39:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/38] mm/gup: fix out-of-bounds write for nr_pages == 0 in
 GUP-fast

With nr_pages == 0, GUP-fast still enters its page table walk and can
write past the caller's page array. The old end <= start check caught
empty ranges, but was replaced with an overflow check.

Users such as OrangeFS can pass a zero page count derived from a
userspace-supplied length. So let's return zero for nr_pages == 0 before
starting the walk, just like GUP-slow.

Fix generated by an LLM and sent by Chris Mason in private.

Fixes: c28b1fc70390 ("mm/gup: reorganize internal_get_user_pages_fast()")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Chris Mason <mason@kernel.org>
[ david: simplify description ]
Reviewed-by: Lorenzo Stoakes (ARM) <ljs@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Muchun Song <muchun.song@linux.dev>
Tested-by: Muhammad Usama Anjum <usama.anjum@arm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261031-fixes_core-v3-21-d6437171ecc3@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: David Hildenbrand (Arm) <david@kernel.org>

(cherry picked from commit 1dfe4b276c23189394afb42d114ee8a54cc3aff2)
[mzak: picked from torvalds master (v7.4-rc2+) for q91n (13 Nov scan, gain A); applies unchanged]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 mm/gup.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/gup.c b/mm/gup.c
index 7d43ce717b24..2018a0e81fb6 100644
--- a/mm/gup.c
+++ b/mm/gup.c
@@ -3211,6 +3211,9 @@ static int gup_fast_fallback(unsigned long start, unsigned long nr_pages,
 				       FOLL_PCI_P2PDMA | FOLL_HONOR_NUMA_FAULT)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (unlikely(!nr_pages))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (gup_flags & FOLL_PIN)
 		mm_set_has_pinned_flag(current->mm);
 
